          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ps-card__foot">
          <canvas id="psBarcode" width="140" height="26" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
          <span class="ps-serial" id="psSerial"></span>
          <button class="ps-card__share" id="psShareCard" type="button"><PixelArtIcon name="share" size="18px" /> tap to share</button>
        </div>
        <span class="ps-stamp" aria-hidden="true">OFFICIAL</span>
      </div>

      <!-- ── 2. UNDER THE CARD: the one sentence that says what this page is for, and where this pass stands on the week's
           plaques — above the tabs, so it is seen whatever pile is open ── -->
      <div class="ps-under">
        <p class="ps-promise">Everything you make and win saves automatically.<noscript> Turn on JavaScript to see it.</noscript></p>
        <p class="ps-week" id="psWeek" hidden><PixelIcon name="sparkle" size="16px" /> <span id="psWeekTxt"></span></p>
      </div>

      <!-- ── 3. YOUR ACCOUNT — one bar, right under the card. ⚠️ the summary carries the sync line, so "Signing you in…" and
           the offline apology are visible whether or not the drawer is open; it opens by itself, email box first, for a pass
           with something to lose that is not logged in. ── -->
      <details class="ps-keep" id="psKeep">
        <summary class="ps-keep__row">
          <PixelArtIcon name="lock" size="22px" />
          <span class="ps-keep__line" id="psSyncNote">Save this to your email later</span>
          <span class="ps-keep__more">Account</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="ps-keep__body">
          <p class="ps-keep__claim" id="psKeepClaim" hidden></p>
          <ul class="ps-perks" id="psPerks">
            <li>No password</li>
            <li>Any device</li>
            <li>Keeps everything you've made</li>
          </ul>
          <form class="ps-mail" id="psMailForm">
            <input class="ps-mail__in" id="psMailIn" type="email" name="email" required
                   autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" spellcheck="false" maxlength="160"
                   placeholder="you@email.com" aria-label="Your email" />
            <button class="btn btn--dark" id="psMailGo" type="submit">Log in</button>
          </form>
          <!-- ⚠️ only shown once somebody is signed in: the same field ADDS an
               address to their pass, so a second person on a shared tablet must
               be told before they type theirs -->
          <p class="ps-mail__whose" id="psMailWhose" hidden></p>

          <!-- passkeys are a SHORTCUT, not a fork you have to understand — and
               the device-code box lives behind the same disclosure, because on
               its own it is a second unexplained way in -->
          <details class="ps-alt" id="psAlt" hidden>
            <summary>Other ways in</summary>
            <div class="ps-sync__row">
              <button class="btn btn--light" id="psSave" type="button"><PixelArtIcon name="save" size="18px" /> Set up on this device</button>
              <button class="btn btn--light" id="psRestore" type="button"><PixelArtIcon name="download" size="18px" /> Use it to log in</button>
            </div>
            <label class="ps-link__lbl" for="psCodeIn">Got a code from your other device?</label>
            <div class="ps-link__row">
              <input class="ps-link__in" id="psCodeIn" type="text" inputmode="latin" autocomplete="off"
                     spellcheck="false" maxlength="12" placeholder="ABCD2468" aria-label="Link code" />
              <button class="btn btn--dark" id="psCodeGo" type="button">Link</button>
            </div>
          </details>

          <!-- 🔗 the answer to a passkey that cannot travel (Windows Hello) -->
          <div class="ps-link" id="psLink" hidden>
            <button class="btn btn--light" id="psLinkStart" type="button"><PixelArtIcon name="link" size="18px" /> Link another device</button>
            <div class="ps-link__code" id="psLinkCode" hidden>
              <b id="psLinkCodeVal">…</b>
              <span id="psLinkCodeHint">type this on the other device</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ps-out ps-disc" id="psDiscordRow" hidden>
            <span class="ps-disc__name" id="psDiscordName"></span>
            <button class="ps-out__btn" id="psDiscordUnlink" type="button"></button>
          </div>
          <div class="ps-out" id="psOut" hidden>
            <button class="ps-out__btn" id="psLogout" type="button">Log out</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- ── 4. NEWS FOR YOU — verdicts on your things and the world's news. Unread ones stand; the ones you have read wait
           behind a single row (renderNews). ── -->
      <section class="ps-news" id="psNewsSec" hidden>
        <h2 class="ps-h" id="psNewsH" hidden><PixelArtIcon name="bell" size="22px" /> News for you</h2>
        <div id="psNotices"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ── 5. YOUR THINGS — three tabs over three panes. ⚠️ THE ZERO STATE HAS NO NAVIGATION: a newcomer gets doors, not
           three empty drawers and a wall of zeros. ── -->
      <section class="ps-things" aria-label="Your things">
        <div class="ps-nav" id="psNav" role="tablist" aria-label="Your pass" hidden>
          <button class="ps-tab" role="tab" id="tab-made" data-tab="made" aria-controls="panel-made" aria-selected="true"><PixelArtIcon name="image" size="22px" /> Made</button>
          <button class="ps-tab" role="tab" id="tab-earned" data-tab="earned" aria-controls="panel-earned" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1"><PixelArtIcon name="trophy" size="22px" /> Earned</button>
          <button class="ps-tab" role="tab" id="tab-numbers" data-tab="numbers" aria-controls="panel-numbers" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1" hidden><PixelArtIcon name="chart-column-increasing" size="22px" /> Stats</button>
        </div>

        <div class="ps-panes" id="psPanes">
          <div class="ps-doors" id="psZero" hidden>
            <a class="ps-door" href="/make-a-banana/"><Nana /><b>Make a banana</b><span>→</span></a>
            <a class="ps-door" href="/forge/"><PixelIcon name="bolt" size="24px" /><b>Forge an emoji</b><span>→</span></a>
            <a class="ps-door" href="/forge/items/"><PixelIcon name="palette" size="24px" /><b>Make an item</b><span>→</span></a>
          </div>

          <section class="ps-pane" role="tabpanel" id="panel-made" aria-labelledby="tab-made" tabindex="0" hidden>
            <!-- chips appear only when two kinds are actually non-empty; with one
                 kind the heading carries the count -->
            <div class="ps-chips" id="psMadeChips" role="group" aria-label="Filter what you made" hidden>
              <button class="ps-chip" type="button" data-kind="" data-h="Everything you've made" aria-pressed="true">All</button>
              <button class="ps-chip" type="button" data-kind="banana" data-h="Bananas" aria-pressed="false" hidden>Bananas</button>
              <button class="ps-chip" type="button" data-kind="wearable" data-h="Items" aria-pressed="false" hidden>Items</button>
              <button class="ps-chip" type="button" data-kind="emoji" data-h="GIFs &amp; emotes" aria-pressed="false" hidden>GIFs</button>
            </div>
            <h2 class="ps-pane__h" id="psMadeH">Everything you've made</h2>
            <div class="ps-shelf" id="psMade"></div>
            <div id="psOffer"></div>

            <!-- 🏷 SEPARATE FROM THE SHELF ON PURPOSE. The shelf above is your
                 sketchbook, kept on this device; this is what other people can
                 actually get hold of. They are different things and the shelf
                 cannot answer "is mine live" — it identifies a creation by its
                 pixels, so an edit would sit beside the original as a near
                 duplicate. Hidden entirely until you have something out there. -->
            <section id="psLiveBlock" hidden>
              <h2 class="ps-pane__h">Out in the world</h2>
              <p class="ps-note">Items of yours that other people can get. Only you can change them.</p>
              <div id="psLive"></div>
            </section>
          </section>

          <!-- GEAR FIRST: it is the thing you DO here. Badges are a trophy case. -->
          <section class="ps-pane" role="tabpanel" id="panel-earned" aria-labelledby="tab-earned" tabindex="0" hidden>
            <div class="ps-chips" role="group" aria-label="Filter what you earned">
              <button class="ps-chip" type="button" data-blk="psGearBlock" aria-pressed="true">Gear</button>
              <button class="ps-chip" type="button" data-blk="psBadgeBlock" aria-pressed="false">Badges</button>
            </div>
            <div id="psGearBlock">
              <h2 class="ps-pane__h" id="psGearH">Gear</h2>
              <div class="ps-gear" id="psGear"></div>
            </div>
            <div id="psBadgeBlock" hidden>
              <h2 class="ps-pane__h" id="psBadgeH">Badges</h2>
              <div class="ps-patches">
                {PATCHES.map((p) => (
                  <div class="ps-patch" data-patch={p.id}>
                    {p.icon === 'nana' ? <Nana /> : <PixelIcon name={p.icon} size="40px" />}
                    <h3>{p.title}</h3>
                    <p>{p.hint}</p>
                    <span class="ps-patch__date"></span>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="ps-pane" role="tabpanel" id="panel-numbers" aria-labelledby="tab-numbers" tabindex="0" hidden>
            <div class="ps-stats">
              {NUMBERS.map((n) => (
                <div class="ps-stat" data-stat={n.k} data-free={n.free ? '1' : null} data-noshare={n.noshare ? '1' : null}>
                  <b>0</b><span>{n.label}</span><i>{n.hint}</i>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ── 6. YOUR SUPPORT — only rendered for a live member. NOT a tab: the
           way to cancel must never be something you hunt for. ── -->
      <section class="ps-sup" id="psSup" hidden>
        <div class="ps-sup__head">
          <img class="ps-sup__hat" id="psSupHat" src="/assets/supporters/hat-blue.png" alt="" width="34" height="31" />
          <div>
            <p class="ps-sup__kicker">your support</p>
            <h2 class="ps-sup__tier" id="psSupTier">Friend of the Banana</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="ps-sup__meta" id="psSupMeta"></p>
        <div class="ps-sup__acts" id="psSupActs">
          <button class="ps-sup__manage" id="psSupCancel" type="button">Cancel membership</button>
          <a class="ps-sup__wall" id="psSupPortal" href="#" rel="noopener">Card &amp; receipts →</a>
          <a class="ps-sup__wall" href="/support/">See the wall</a>
        </div>
        <!-- the confirm opens IN the card. A membership's exit does not deserve
             a modal on top of the page it lives on. -->
        <div class="ps-sup__ask" id="psSupAsk" hidden>
          <p class="ps-sup__askt" id="psSupAskT"></p>
          <label class="ps-sup__why">If you like, say why <small>(optional)</small>
            <select id="psSupWhy">
              <option value="">—</option>
              <option value="too_expensive">Too expensive</option>
              <option value="unused">I wasn't using it</option>
              <option value="missing_features">Missing something I wanted</option>
              <option value="low_quality">Not what I hoped</option>
              <option value="switched_service">Supporting something else</option>
              <option value="other">Another reason</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <div class="ps-sup__askrow">
            <button class="ps-sup__yes" id="psSupYes" type="button">Yes, cancel it</button>
            <button class="ps-sup__no" id="psSupNo" type="button">Never mind</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="ps-sup__note" id="psSupNote" hidden></p>
        <p class="ps-sup__miss" id="psSupMiss" hidden>We can't see which membership this is from this login — it was probably paid with a different email address. Sign in with that one and the button appears here, or use the link above.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- ── 7. THE DOORS OUT ── -->
      <div class="ps-doors" id="psDoors">
        <a class="ps-door" id="psDoorMake" href="/make-a-banana/"><Nana /><b>Make a banana</b><span>→</span></a>
        <a class="ps-door ps-door--out" href="/rave/"><PixelIcon name="sparkle" size="24px" /><b>To the dancefloor</b><span>→</span></a>
      </div>

      <!-- ── 8. THE ASK — the newsletter, last: earned by having something here or news above, never next to the login ── -->
      <details class="ps-ask" id="psAsk" hidden>
        <summary class="ps-ask__row"><PixelArtIcon name="mail" size="20px" /> Want a note when the world gets bigger?</summary>
        <form id="psAskForm">
          <p id="psAskLead">New areas, features, items and the odd bit of merch — one click unsubscribes.</p>
          <div class="ps-mail" id="psAskMail">
            <input class="ps-mail__in" id="psNewsIn" type="email" name="news" required
                   autocomplete="email" inputmode="email" spellcheck="false" maxlength="160"
                   placeholder="you@email.com" aria-label="Email for updates" />
            <button class="btn btn--light" id="psNewsGo" type="submit">Keep me posted</button>
          </div>
          <p class="ps-ask__note" id="psNewsNote"></p>
        </form>
      </details>
  </div>

  <!-- share-card lightbox: our own reveal, the rave-card pattern in pass colours -->
  <div class="ps-sharemodal" id="psShareModal" hidden>
    <div class="ps-sharemodal__box">
      <button class="ps-sharemodal__close" id="psShareClose" aria-label="Close"><PixelArtIcon name="close" size="18px" /></button>
      <div class="ps-sharemodal__card" id="psShareSlot"></div>
      <div class="ps-sharemodal__row">
        <button class="btn btn--dark" id="psShareDl"><PixelArtIcon name="download" size="18px" /> Download PNG</button>
        <button class="btn btn--light" id="psShareCopy"><PixelArtIcon name="copy" size="18px" /> Copy image</button>
        <button class="btn btn--light" id="psShareSys" hidden><PixelArtIcon name="share" size="18px" /> Share…</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/banana-pass-page.js';
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
